<!-- Next Transfer notification small icon — owner decision (2026-09-22), final.

     WHY THIS ARTWORK.  Android's small-icon slot is a monochrome ALPHA MASK: the
     system discards RGB, recolours the alpha with the notification tint and never
     draws a background.  The owner reviewed the previous simplified notebook page
     and rejected it twice over: the left glyph read as a generic document rather
     than as Next Transfer, and the full-colour app logo that had been attached on
     the right of the card (as `largeIcon`) was not wanted either.  The approved
     Next Transfer mark is HANDS HANDING OFF THE PLANNER, so this redraw carries
     that handover INSIDE the legal small-icon form: a tilted notebook page gripped
     at its lower corners by two mirrored hands.

     HOW IT IS BUILT.  Three solid white paths on a 24x24 viewport — no strokes, no
     line art, no gradients, no groups and no transforms (every rotation is baked
     into the coordinates, so nothing can drift at render time):
       1. the page  — one path filled `evenOdd`, so the binding channel and the
                      three writing lines are transparent CUT-OUTS of the same
                      shape rather than extra tinted shapes;
       2. the hands — one path each, filled `nonZero`, each a union of a palm, two
                      staggered fingers and an angled thumb.  `nonZero` is what
                      lets those four rounded parts MERGE into a single gesture
                      while the outline keeps the finger notches that make a hand
                      readable once the icon is downscaled and tinted.
     The fingertips rise just past the page's lower edge on both sides: that small
     overlap is what reads as a grip rather than as three separate objects.

     SCALE AND INSET.  The mark occupies roughly x 2.9..21.0 and y 2.3..21.0, i.e.
     a margin of two units or more on every side, so no platform mask and no OEM
     circular backdrop can clip it.  Nothing thinner than ~0.9 units is used, so no
     detail collapses into noise at status-bar size.

     RESOURCE CONTRACT — all deliberately unchanged:
       * the resource NAME stays `ic_nt_notification`, because the Dart plugin
         resolves it by name at runtime and `res/raw/keep.xml` is what stops the
         release resource shrinker from stripping it;
       * 24dp x 24dp, transparent background, one monochrome white fill colour.
     NO large icon is configured anywhere (owner decision, 2026-09-22): the card
     shows the system small icon and the notification text only. -->
